  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi Donor Trust Fund for the Pacific Region Infrastructure Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The Pacific Regional Infrastructure Facility is a multi-donor  partnership established to provide flexible, transparent long-term  support and increased infrastructure investment in Pacific Island  Countries. This TFP represents interim funding arrangements for funds  administered by the World Bank.  In parallel, AusAID is also  establishing a separate Infrastructure Facility administered by ADB.   These Facilities will be administered separately but with common  mechanisms to ensure effective coordination.
 
 During this interim phase, a longer-term PRIF funding and delivery  mechanism will be developed, with the interim process providing the  development partners an opportunity to strengthen coordination and  harmonization, as well as undertake core analytic work to define a  long-term strategic direction.
 
 PRIF has five overall strategic objectives:
 1. Strengthen infrastructure services through the provision of  long-term, performance-linked support.
 2. Support country and region-led mechanisms, including infrastructure  planning and management and enhanced country/regional ownership.
 3. Support public expenditure management, by assisting with improved  budgetary management and planning/funding of infrastructure services.
 4. Build technical and institutional capacity to manage infrastructure,  with a focus on approaches suitable for small island states.
 5. Improve partnership and harmonization, by providing a common  platform for collaboration in infrastructure in the Pacific.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
